          "code": "DISPLAY_WIDGET_DATA",
          "id": "1767173301814",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767173301815_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: {{$context.$nodes.SKILLS_RECOMMENDER_WF_AGENT.$output.output}} \n\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Employee Skills Recommendations to be added to the profile based on previous gig and learning history or the current role and aspirational roles for typical career progression. These are skill additions that the user can update in their profile for better insights.\nYou must adhere to the standard oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.\n\n**DIRECTIVE:**\nYour sole purpose is to transform input data about available skills for employees into a valid <oraInfoDisplay> XML block using the messageListWidget.\n\n**ROOT CONFIGURATION:**\n\ntitle: Generate a concise headline (e.g., \"Skills Profile Summary and Recommendations\").\ndescription: Generate a short, non-repetitive summary explaining the value of updating these skills in the profile. If there is no previous gig and learning history, indicate that completing a gig or learning activity will automatically surface skills to add. Also, DO include a sentence indicating when the profile was last updated using the input received.\n\n**STRICT MAPPING RULES:**\nGenerate a messageListWidget with the below items\nItem 1\ntitle: \"Current Skills\"\nsummary: a comma-separated list of currentSkills (names only, no extra text). If no skills available, indicate in second person reference that the user's profile does not have skills updated and encourage user to update skills for better opportunity matches.\nDo not include badgeText\n\nItem 2\ntitle: \"Additional Skills to Add\"\nsummary: one concise sentence indicating the source and readiness to add, followed by a comma-separated list of skills:\nIf gig or course skills is non-empty, mention concisely whether the skills are demonstrated in the completed gigs or learning activities and ready to add: {comma-separated gigCourseSkills}. Include the sources as gigs or learning activities depending on the sources the skills are derived from and do not include the name of the gig or course.\nElse if role based skills is non-empty: “Derived from your current and aspirational roles and recommended to add: {comma-separated roleBasedSkills}.”\nElse: “No additional skills available yet; completing a gig or learning activity will surface skills you can readily add.”\nbadgeText: Use “NEW” only if gig and course skills is non-empty; omit badgeText otherwise.\n\nitems[].title: Map the skill name here. For current skills display \"Current Skills\" as the title\nitems[].summary: Map a strictly one sentence, concise summary of the title field here. This should indicate if the skill is demonstrated in the gig or the course the user has completed and can be added in the profile or if it is derived based on roles. For current skills display a comma separated list of skills and include only the skill names.\nitems[].badgeText: Use the badge as NEW only if the skill source is a gig or course, do not show a badge if the source is role based.\n\nDo not include priority, timestamp, or image for any item."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Summary LLM for Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARY_LLM_FOR_WIDGET",
          "id": "1767683733004",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767683733005_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Following output contains a list of skills suggested to the user to add to the profile so that the applications can suggest matching opportunities and analyze current skill gaps to aspirational roles. Generate a summary indicating if these are demonstrated skills from recent gig or learning activity. If the source is not recent activity the skills are derived from the current role and any favorite aspirational roles. Always use second person when referring to the user. If the source is not recent activity, indicate that there is no recent gig or learning completion recorded yet and encourage the user to update the skills in their profile if they've acquired any of these skills, in this case also mention that completing a gig or learning activity will automatically suggest skills that can be readily updated in profile.\n\nAlso, DO include a sentence indicating when the profile was last updated using the input received.\n\nDo not show any additional thinking/explanation. Only display a summary of max two to three sentences.\n\n{{$context.$nodes.SKILLS_RECOMMENDER_WF_AGENT.$output.output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
