          },
          "code": "ACTION_LLM_FOR_WIDGET",
          "id": "1767776492244",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767776492247_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the final InitActions normalizer for the Skills Profile widget in the Career Advancement Command Center.\n\nAction candidates from the action workflow:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_DATA_FOR_INIT_ACTIONS_AGENT.$output.result}}\n\nRaw skills profile recommendation data:\n{{$context.$nodes.SKILLS_RECOMMENDER_WF_AGENT.$output.output}}\n\nYour job is to return widget-level action insights the app can render.\n\nRendering contract:\n- Return raw oraInsight blocks only.\n- Do not return a JSON array.\n- Do not return markdown, prose, code fences, or a wrapper object.\n- Do not quote the whole response as a string.\n- If there are no recommended additional skills, return nothing at all.\n- If there are recommended additional skills, return exactly one oraInsight block.\n\nPrimary source:\n- Prefer a valid action candidate from the action workflow when present.\n- If the action workflow output is empty, derive the Add Skills action directly from the raw skills profile recommendation data.\n\nSkill extraction fallback:\n- Look for arrays named newSkillRecommendations, gigCourseSkills, roleBasedSkills, additionalSkills, skillsToAdd, recommendedSkills, or similar.\n- If an item is an object, use Skill, skill, SkillName, name, title, or label as the skill name.\n- Exclude skills that are already present in currentSkills.\n- De-duplicate skill names case-insensitively.\n- Keep at most 15 skills in the payload.\n- Do not invent skill names.\n\nOutput format:\n<oraInsight>\n{\n  \"title\": \"Add Skills to Profile\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Add recommended skills to improve opportunity matching.\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Add Skills\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"ADDSKILLS\\\",{\\\"actionCode\\\":\\\"ADDSKILLS\\\",\\\"skills\\\":[\\\"<skill1>\\\",\\\"<skill2>\\\"]})\"\n}\n</oraInsight>\n\nRules:\n- Use action code ADDSKILLS exactly.\n- The block body must be valid JSON.\n- JSON-escape all double quotes inside followUpCommand.\n- Do not include priority.\n- Do not include any text outside the oraInsight block."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "outputSpecification": ""
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
