          },
          "code": "FORMAT_RESPONSE_FOR_WIDGET",
          "id": "1767793367422",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767793367423_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: `{{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_SKILLS_PROFILE_ACTIONS.$output.output}}`\n\"You are generating an information display for an Agentic App. The action result will conform to the following JSON schema, output exactly one escaped <oraInfoDisplay> element (no additional text, explanation, or markdown). Follow these instructions precisely:\n\nIf the result matches the Schema (has 'message' and 'skills'):\nOutput a single escaped <oraInfoDisplay> with key 'unique:profileupdate{skills}'.\nUse patternId 'cardWidget'.\nThe JSON payload properties must include:\ntitle: Skills update\npatternId: 'cardWidget'\ndescription: a one-line summary (use the 'message' value)\nproperties: an object matching the cardWidget schema:\nsubject: Skills updated in profile\ntimestamp: Just now,\nbadgeText: SUCCESS,\nsummary: message\nvariant: 'info'\nExample output shape:\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"unique:profileupdate{skills}\">\n{ \"title\": \"...\", \"patternId\":\"cardWidget\", \"description\":\"...\", \"properties\": { \"subject\":\"...\", \"summary\":\"...\", \"variant\":\"info\" } }\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n\nGeneral rules:\nOutput only one escaped <oraInfoDisplay> element (no surrounding text).\nUse the widget patternIds exactly: 'cardWidget'\nKeep titles concise and descriptions short.\nDo not fabricate missing recipient or linking data. Omit optional fields if they are not present in the input.\nDo not include any XML that is not the single escaped <oraInfoDisplay> element.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nERROR HANDLING\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nIf the output {{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_SKILLS_PROFILE_ACTIONS.$output.output}} contains the text \"Error occurred on this action\": return the below as palin text\n\nThe action could not be completed. Please try again."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Use the Messages List widget when there is more than one item in the response, otherwise format the output appropriately."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query Response for Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY_RESPONSE_FOR_WIDGET",
          "id": "1767800428361",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767800428363_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "User Query : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nChat History: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nYour task is to answer only if the user’s query is directly related to the user’s current role, skills, or suggested skills, and their respective sources as provided below.\nDo not answer any other question. If a query is not about these topics, reply:\n\"I can only answer questions related to your current and suggested skills and their sources, based on the provided information.\"\nOnly use the following data:\nCurrent role, skills, and suggested skills: {{$context.$nodes.SKILLS_RECOMMENDER_WF_AGENT.$output.output}} \n\nThe answer to the query must be based on the data available to you which contains the user's current skills and suggested new skills to add to profile along with the source from which the skill was derived. If the type is a course it indicates that the user is already developing the skill and has completed the course. If it's a gig, the user would have used that skill while working on that gig. Do NOT suggest any learning opportunities if asked about the suggested or current skill as that information is not available in the data given.\n\nFor the suggested skills, if the type is either gig or course it indicates user's familiarity with the corresponding skill by completing the course or the gig in such cases do not recommend the same course or gig to the user for further skill enhancement. In some cases the suggested skills may be associated with an aspirational role for which the skill is a requirement in which case there is no evidence of the user's familiarity with the skill, answer the questions accordingly. If the question cannot be answered with the available data indicate it to the user.\n\nFormat and output the items in your response with all the details available. Use chat history to get any previous context. If there are multiple items then do the same for all items and output them as a visually clear list for the user. Use Bold and italics to highlight fields and make it easy to scan. Take the necessary relevant information to support your answer. Consider the chat history to get previous context if needed."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Subtitle"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_SUBTITLE",
          "id": "1768374579640",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768374579642_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a fresh welcome message when the user logs in. \nAlways greet the user by name using {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}}. \nDo not ask questions, do not request clarification, and do not explain anything. \nOutput should be a short, friendly welcome message."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check For Empty Data"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1770058252053",
            "false": "add_false_1770058164809"
